estions for other owners, which I will carry into their notes. Q1 (contract successor d56d7f65 with authority 406983fe): confirm that a runtime without the capability records answers unsupported-definition for both lanes, and say whether tests may use a scripted test capability, wired and labelled like I1's test authority. One step waits on this. Q2: adopt or reject revision 12's answer to G27; until then I2 fails closed. Q3: record the one count of 35 sends and 33 results. Q4: how an entry records a party list set whole. Q5: may a declared definition state a name beginning platform:. Q6 (lane forms): renew-hold in change after a merge, and what ends a timed-out job nobody answers.\n\nThe plan's author also read the landed I1 source and named places that look wrong. I will confirm each before acting: an absent optional field empties a slot (derive effects.ts), where the contract says it is not applied; a relate with no matching handler is applied and a copy kept (derive delivery.ts); a fact guard cannot name a genesis entry (derive guards.ts); two bounds have values that no source reads (contract bounds.ts); an index row goes to the creator rather than the directory (derive sends.ts). Each confirmed one is repaired inside I2 where its step touches it, or filed as its own small request."}